WEBVTT

00:02.467 --> 00:03.885
KATARA: Water.

00:04.761 --> 00:06.137
Earth.

00:06.763 --> 00:08.097
Fire.

00:08.890 --> 00:10.141
Air.

00:11.184 --> 00:15.146
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.396 --> 00:18.608
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.651 --> 00:22.529
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.612 --> 00:23.821
could stop them.

00:23.905 --> 00:26.574
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:27.367 --> 00:29.827
100 years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

00:29.911 --> 00:32.705
the new Avatar,
an airbender named Aang.

00:32.956 --> 00:35.083
And although
his airbending skills are great,

00:35.166 --> 00:37.752
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.835 --> 00:38.920
AANG: Oof.

00:39.128 --> 00:42.090
KATARA: But I believe
Aang can save the world.

01:00.737 --> 01:01.905
( CHIRPS )

01:03.949 --> 01:05.283
( GASPS )

01:07.869 --> 01:11.748
Waterbending bomb! Yeah!

01:13.041 --> 01:15.126
( SPLASH )

01:15.210 --> 01:16.586
( ICE SHATTERS )

01:16.670 --> 01:17.754
( LAUGHING )

01:17.837 --> 01:20.924
Sure, 5,000-year-old maps
from the Spirit Library.

01:21.007 --> 01:23.009
Just splash some water on them.

01:23.593 --> 01:25.095
Sorry.

01:25.220 --> 01:27.430
( BIRDS CHIRPING )

01:30.600 --> 01:32.936
So did you figure out
what route we're gonna take?

01:33.019 --> 01:36.314
SOKKA: Okay, we just got out of
the desert, so we must be around here.

01:36.398 --> 01:38.608
And we need to go to
Ba Sing Se, which is here.

01:38.692 --> 01:41.695
It looks like the only passage
connecting the south to the north

01:41.778 --> 01:44.072
is this sliver of land
called the Serpent's Pass.

01:44.155 --> 01:47.200
- You're sure that's the best way to go?
- It's the only way.

01:47.284 --> 01:49.744
I mean, it's not like we
have Appa to fly us there.

01:49.828 --> 01:51.162
Shush up about Appa.

01:51.288 --> 01:53.707
Can't you at least
try to be sensitive?

01:55.083 --> 01:56.835
Katara, it's okay.

01:56.918 --> 01:59.212
I know I was upset about
losing Appa before,

01:59.296 --> 02:01.798
but I just want to focus on
getting to Ba Sing Se

02:01.881 --> 02:04.718
and telling the Earth King
about the solar eclipse.

02:05.343 --> 02:09.597
Oh, well, okay.
I'm glad you're doing better.

02:09.681 --> 02:12.475
Then to Ba Sing Se we go.
No more distractions.

02:12.559 --> 02:14.936
Hello there, fellow refugees!

02:19.649 --> 02:22.068
So are you guys headed
to Ba Sing Se too?

02:22.152 --> 02:23.278
Sure are.

02:23.361 --> 02:26.281
We're trying to get there before
my wife, Ying, has her baby.

02:26.364 --> 02:29.034
Great. We can travel through
the Serpent's Pass together.

02:29.576 --> 02:31.411
The Serpent's Pass?

02:31.494 --> 02:34.122
Only the truly desperate
take that deadly route.

02:34.205 --> 02:37.083
Deadly route? Great pick, Sokka!

02:37.167 --> 02:38.668
Well, we are desperate.

02:38.752 --> 02:40.920
You should come with us to Full Moon Bay.

02:41.004 --> 02:43.423
Ferries take refugees
across the lake.

02:43.506 --> 02:45.842
It's the fastest
way to Ba Sing Se.

02:45.925 --> 02:48.845
And it's hidden so the Fire Nation
can't find it.

02:49.220 --> 02:52.557
Hmm, peaceful ferry ride or deadly pass?

03:02.442 --> 03:04.319
I can't believe how many people's lives

03:04.402 --> 03:06.446
have been uprooted
by the Fire Nation.

03:06.529 --> 03:08.365
We're all looking for a better life...

03:08.448 --> 03:09.449
( BABY CRIES )

03:09.532 --> 03:11.618
...safe behind the walls
of Ba Sing Se.

03:22.003 --> 03:24.672
Who would've thought
after all these years

03:24.756 --> 03:26.716
I'd return to the scene

03:26.800 --> 03:31.388
of my greatest military disgrace
as a tourist?

03:31.471 --> 03:32.639
Look around.

03:32.722 --> 03:34.933
We're not tourists. We're refugees.

03:36.851 --> 03:38.019
Ugh!

03:38.103 --> 03:40.605
I'm sick of eating rotten food,
sleeping in the dirt.

03:40.688 --> 03:42.524
I'm tired of living like this.

03:42.607 --> 03:43.650
JET: Aren't we all?

03:47.821 --> 03:50.365
My name's Jet, and these
are my Freedom Fighters,

03:50.448 --> 03:52.075
Smellerbee and Longshot.

03:52.158 --> 03:53.159
Hey.

03:54.160 --> 03:55.245
Hello.

03:55.328 --> 03:56.538
Here's the deal.

03:56.621 --> 03:58.540
I hear the captain's eating like a king

03:58.623 --> 04:01.126
while all us refugees have
to feed off his scraps.

04:01.209 --> 04:03.086
Doesn't seem fair, does it?

04:03.169 --> 04:05.797
What sort of king
is he eating like?

04:05.880 --> 04:07.841
The fat, happy kind.

04:09.759 --> 04:12.178
You wanna help us
liberate some food?

04:17.892 --> 04:19.519
-( SPLASHES )
- I'm in.

04:27.068 --> 04:30.029
I told you already,
no vegetables on the ferry!

04:30.363 --> 04:31.656
One cabbage slug

04:31.739 --> 04:34.534
could destroy the entire
ecosystem of Ba Sing Se!

04:34.617 --> 04:36.494
- Security!
- Aah!

04:36.619 --> 04:39.038
( GROWLS )

04:39.164 --> 04:42.542
Gah, my cabbages!

04:42.667 --> 04:45.462
( SOBS )

04:47.547 --> 04:48.840
Next!

04:50.341 --> 04:52.927
Um, four tickets for the
ferry to Ba Sing Se, please.

04:53.052 --> 04:54.262
Passports?

04:54.387 --> 04:57.765
Uh, no one told us we
had to have passports.

04:57.891 --> 05:00.602
Don't you know who this is?
He's the Avatar.

05:00.727 --> 05:02.937
Ah, I see 50 Avatars a day.

05:03.062 --> 05:05.565
And by the way,
not a very impressive costume.

05:09.110 --> 05:10.111
( SQUAWKS )

05:10.195 --> 05:14.449
Besides, no animals allowed.
Do I need to call security?

05:14.991 --> 05:16.826
( BURPS )

05:16.951 --> 05:18.286
( SQUEAKS AND TRILLS )

05:18.411 --> 05:20.246
That won't be necessary.

05:20.371 --> 05:22.707
- Next!
- I'll take care of this.

05:23.791 --> 05:26.836
My name is Toph Beifong
and I need four tickets.

05:27.212 --> 05:31.299
Ah, the golden seal of the flying boar.

05:31.424 --> 05:35.470
It is my pleasure to help
anyone of the Beifong family.

05:35.595 --> 05:37.138
It is your pleasure.

05:37.263 --> 05:38.640
As you can see,

05:38.765 --> 05:41.935
I am blind and these
three imbeciles are my valets.

05:42.060 --> 05:44.979
- But the animal―
- Is my seeing-eye lemur.

05:45.063 --> 05:46.064
( CHATTERS )

05:46.731 --> 05:49.400
Well, normally it's only one ticket
per passport,

05:49.526 --> 05:52.487
but this document
is so official,

05:52.612 --> 05:54.697
I guess it's worth four tickets.

05:57.408 --> 05:58.451
Thank you very much.

05:59.994 --> 06:01.871
All right!
We scammed that lady good!

06:01.996 --> 06:03.414
Aah!

06:03.540 --> 06:06.626
- Tickets and passports, please.
- Is there a problem?

06:06.751 --> 06:08.962
Yeah, I got a problem with you.

06:09.087 --> 06:10.755
I've seen your type before.

06:10.880 --> 06:13.132
Probably sarcastic,
think you're hilarious.

06:13.258 --> 06:16.052
And let me guess,
you're traveling with the Avatar.

06:16.636 --> 06:17.887
Do I know you?

06:18.513 --> 06:21.099
You mean you don't remember?
Maybe you remember this.

06:23.560 --> 06:24.561
Suki!

06:25.937 --> 06:27.647
Sokka, it's good to see you!

06:28.898 --> 06:33.152
KATARA: You look so different
without your makeup and the new outfit.

06:33.236 --> 06:35.947
That crabby lady makes all
the security guards wear them.

06:36.406 --> 06:39.200
And look at you, sleeveless guy.
Been working out?

06:39.284 --> 06:41.786
Oh, I'll grab a tree branch
and do a few chin touches

06:41.869 --> 06:43.997
every now and then. Nothing major.

06:45.707 --> 06:47.584
Are the other Kyoshi Warriors around?

06:47.667 --> 06:51.337
Yeah. After you left Kyoshi,
we wanted to find a way to help people.

06:51.421 --> 06:54.632
We ended up escorting some refugees,
and we've been here ever since.

06:54.757 --> 06:56.134
-( CHATTERS )
-( LAUGHS )

06:56.217 --> 06:58.094
Hi, Momo. Good to see you too.

06:58.177 --> 06:59.470
( TRILLS )

06:59.554 --> 07:01.931
So why are you guys getting
tickets for the ferry?

07:02.015 --> 07:03.808
Wouldn't you just fly across on Appa?

07:05.226 --> 07:06.603
Appa is missing.

07:06.728 --> 07:09.022
We hope to find him in Ba Sing Se.

07:09.147 --> 07:12.650
I'm so sorry to hear that.
Are you doing okay?

07:16.529 --> 07:17.697
I'm doing fine.

07:17.822 --> 07:19.782
Would everybody stop
worrying about me?

07:19.907 --> 07:22.744
Avatar Aang, you have to help us!

07:22.869 --> 07:24.746
Someone took all of our belongings,

07:24.871 --> 07:28.708
our passports, our tickets.
Everything's gone!

07:28.791 --> 07:29.792
( SOBS )

07:29.876 --> 07:31.544
I'll talk to the lady for you.

07:33.046 --> 07:35.006
No passports, no tickets!

07:36.466 --> 07:38.926
But she's pregnant, and
all their stuff was stolen.

07:39.010 --> 07:40.637
You have to make an exception.

07:40.720 --> 07:41.888
No exceptions!

07:42.221 --> 07:44.682
If I just gave away tickets
willy-nilly to anyone,

07:44.766 --> 07:46.392
there would be no more order.

07:46.476 --> 07:49.270
And you know what that means―
no more civilization!

07:49.354 --> 07:50.897
What if we gave
them our tickets?

07:50.980 --> 07:51.981
- No!
- But―

07:52.065 --> 07:53.066
- Next!
-( SPITS )

07:54.317 --> 07:56.819
Don't worry, you'll
get to the city safely.

07:57.236 --> 07:59.197
I'll lead you through the Serpent's Pass.

08:06.871 --> 08:08.706
I can't believe we gave up our tickets

08:08.790 --> 08:11.000
and now we're going through
the Serpent's Pass.

08:11.084 --> 08:13.419
I can't believe you're
still complaining about it.

08:13.503 --> 08:14.504
I'm coming too!

08:15.880 --> 08:17.632
Are you sure that's a good idea?

08:17.715 --> 08:19.592
Sokka, I thought you'd want me to come.

08:19.717 --> 08:20.718
I do. It's just―

08:20.843 --> 08:22.470
Just what?

08:22.595 --> 08:24.180
Nothing. I'm glad you're coming.

08:29.310 --> 08:31.187
This is the Serpent's Pass?

08:31.270 --> 08:32.897
I thought it would be more wind-y.

08:32.980 --> 08:36.109
You know, like a serpent.
Hmm, I guess they misnamed it.

08:36.192 --> 08:39.028
Look at this writing. How awful.

08:39.112 --> 08:40.363
What does it say?

08:40.613 --> 08:42.782
It says, "Abandon hope."

08:43.408 --> 08:46.994
How could we abandon hope?
That's all we have.

08:47.120 --> 08:48.621
AANG: I don't know.

08:48.746 --> 08:51.582
The monks used to say that hope
is just a distraction.

08:51.708 --> 08:53.751
So maybe we do need to abandon it.

08:53.876 --> 08:55.253
What are you talking about?

08:56.129 --> 08:58.172
Hope isn't going to
get us into Ba Sing Se,

08:58.297 --> 09:00.007
and it's not gonna find Appa.

09:00.508 --> 09:02.760
We need to focus on what
we're doing right now,

09:02.844 --> 09:04.721
and that's getting across this pass.

09:06.681 --> 09:08.725
Okay, if you say so.

09:13.980 --> 09:16.232
SUKI: The Fire Nation
controls the Western Lake.

09:16.315 --> 09:19.277
Rumor has it they're working on
something big on the other side

09:19.360 --> 09:21.696
and they don't want anyone
to find out what it is.

09:27.285 --> 09:28.286
Whoa!

09:28.369 --> 09:29.412
( GROANS )

09:31.539 --> 09:32.540
I'm okay!

09:33.124 --> 09:34.208
( RUMBLING )

09:34.292 --> 09:35.710
( SPLASH )

09:37.128 --> 09:38.129
They spotted us!

09:38.212 --> 09:39.380
Let's go! Let's go!

09:43.801 --> 09:45.344
( BLASTS )

09:48.681 --> 09:49.682
( GASPS )

09:56.397 --> 09:58.191
Suki, are you okay?

09:58.274 --> 10:00.526
You have to be more careful!
Come on!

10:01.694 --> 10:03.279
Thanks for saving my life, Toph.

10:03.362 --> 10:05.281
Hey, no problem, Sokka.

10:21.255 --> 10:23.466
Suki, you shouldn't
sleep there.

10:23.549 --> 10:25.176
Who knows how stable
this ledge is?

10:25.259 --> 10:26.803
It could give way at any moment.

10:26.886 --> 10:28.930
Sokka, I'm fine.
Stop worrying!

10:29.013 --> 10:30.640
You're right, you're right.

10:30.723 --> 10:33.184
You're perfectly capable
of taking care of yourself.

10:33.267 --> 10:34.393
Wait!

10:34.477 --> 10:37.230
Oh, never mind.
I thought I saw a spider. But you're fine.

11:10.805 --> 11:12.098
SMELLERBEE: Guard's coming!

11:32.702 --> 11:35.079
You know, it's okay to miss Appa.

11:36.831 --> 11:38.291
What's going on with you?

11:38.374 --> 11:40.835
In the desert, all you cared
about was finding Appa.

11:40.918 --> 11:43.254
And now it's like you don't
care about him at all.

11:43.337 --> 11:45.172
You saw what I did out there.

11:45.298 --> 11:48.759
I was so angry about losing
Appa, I couldn't control myself.

11:48.885 --> 11:50.636
I hated feeling like that.

11:50.761 --> 11:53.556
But now you're not letting
yourself feel anything.

11:53.681 --> 11:56.058
I know sometimes
it hurts more to hope,

11:56.183 --> 11:58.561
and it hurts more to care.

11:58.686 --> 12:01.230
But you have to promise me
that you won't stop caring.

12:02.815 --> 12:04.317
Come on, you need a hug.

12:05.818 --> 12:07.737
AANG: Thank you for you concern, Katara.

12:21.584 --> 12:24.170
- It's a beautiful moon.
- Yeah, it really is.

12:26.797 --> 12:28.716
Look, I know you're just trying to help,

12:28.841 --> 12:30.676
but I can take care of myself.

12:30.801 --> 12:32.053
I know you can.

12:32.178 --> 12:34.472
Then why are you
acting so overprotective?

12:34.555 --> 12:37.016
It's so hard to lose
someone you care about.

12:37.099 --> 12:38.893
Something happened at the North Pole

12:38.976 --> 12:40.686
and I couldn't protect someone.

12:40.770 --> 12:43.272
I don't want anything like
that to ever happen again.

12:43.356 --> 12:45.316
I lost someone I cared about.

12:45.441 --> 12:48.235
He didn't die. He just went away.

12:48.361 --> 12:50.488
I only had a few days
to get to know him,

12:50.613 --> 12:54.367
but he was smart,
and brave, and funny.

12:54.492 --> 12:57.662
Who is this guy?
Is he taller than me?

12:57.787 --> 12:59.664
No, he's about your height.

12:59.789 --> 13:02.792
- Is he better-looking?
- It is you, stupid!

13:02.917 --> 13:04.251
Oh.

13:11.968 --> 13:13.219
I can't.

13:13.844 --> 13:15.096
I'm sorry.

13:16.681 --> 13:18.766
No, you shouldn't be.

13:27.233 --> 13:29.694
So, Smellerbee.

13:29.777 --> 13:32.738
That's an unusual name for a young man.

13:32.905 --> 13:34.782
Maybe it's because I'm not a man.

13:34.907 --> 13:36.325
I'm a girl!

13:37.576 --> 13:39.912
Oh, now I see!

13:40.037 --> 13:43.207
It's a beautiful name for a lovely girl!

13:46.252 --> 13:48.170
I know. You're right.

13:48.295 --> 13:50.214
As long as I'm confident with who I am,

13:50.339 --> 13:52.550
it doesn't matter what
other people think.

13:52.675 --> 13:53.843
Thanks, Longshot.

13:56.429 --> 13:57.430
( SLURPING )

13:57.513 --> 13:58.931
From what I heard,

13:59.015 --> 14:01.851
people eat like this
every night in Ba Sing Se.

14:01.934 --> 14:04.395
I can't wait to set my
eyes on that giant wall.

14:04.562 --> 14:07.148
It is a magnificent sight.

14:07.273 --> 14:09.150
So you've been there before?

14:09.275 --> 14:13.529
Once, when I was a different man.

14:13.654 --> 14:16.574
I've done some things in my past
that I'm not proud of.

14:16.699 --> 14:19.118
But that's why I'm going to Ba Sing Se,

14:19.243 --> 14:22.371
for a new beginning,
a second chance.

14:22.496 --> 14:25.041
That's very noble of you.

14:25.166 --> 14:28.711
I believe people can change
their lives if they want to.

14:28.836 --> 14:30.713
I believe in second chances.

14:44.143 --> 14:45.394
( MOMO TRILLS )

14:53.110 --> 14:54.278
Everyone single file!

14:55.905 --> 14:57.073
( WATER RUSHING )

15:03.704 --> 15:05.414
KATARA: Aang, I need help!

15:05.790 --> 15:06.791
( CHATTERS )

15:28.646 --> 15:29.647
( FRIGHTENED CHATTER )

15:33.192 --> 15:34.235
What is that thing?

15:35.486 --> 15:36.487
( GASPING )

15:37.863 --> 15:40.366
( SCREAMING )

15:45.121 --> 15:47.081
( SPLASH )

16:02.721 --> 16:06.142
( ROARS )

16:06.225 --> 16:09.353
I think I just figured out why
they call it the Serpent's Pass!

16:10.187 --> 16:11.313
( ROARS )

16:14.775 --> 16:16.235
( ROARS )

16:17.319 --> 16:19.196
Suki, you know about
giant sea monsters.

16:19.280 --> 16:20.656
Make it go away!

16:20.739 --> 16:24.160
Just because I live near the Unagi
doesn't mean I'm an expert!

16:24.243 --> 16:26.620
Oh great and powerful sea serpent,

16:26.704 --> 16:28.914
please accept this humble
and tasty offering.

16:28.998 --> 16:30.666
- Thank you.
- Sokka!

16:31.083 --> 16:34.253
( SCREECHES )

16:34.336 --> 16:36.755
I'll distract it.
Katara, get everyone across.

16:36.839 --> 16:37.840
( ROARS )

16:43.053 --> 16:44.054
( SERPENT ROARS )

16:45.139 --> 16:46.473
( ROARS )

16:46.557 --> 16:47.892
( SCREECHES )

16:52.021 --> 16:53.230
( SCREECHES )

17:03.949 --> 17:05.284
( ROARS )

17:06.535 --> 17:07.536
( SCREECHES )

17:09.163 --> 17:10.623
Toph, come on! It's just ice!

17:13.250 --> 17:17.213
Actually, I'm gonna stay on my
little island where I can see.

17:17.296 --> 17:18.297
( SCREECHES )

17:18.380 --> 17:19.840
Aah! Okay, I'm coming!

17:22.343 --> 17:23.761
SOKKA: You're doing great!

17:23.886 --> 17:27.097
Just follow the sound of my voice.

17:27.181 --> 17:28.724
It's hard to ignore.

17:29.433 --> 17:31.352
SOKKA: You're almost there!

17:31.435 --> 17:33.604
-( SERPENT ROARS )
-( SCREAMS )

17:33.687 --> 17:36.023
Help! I can't swim!

17:37.024 --> 17:38.400
SOKKA: I'm coming, Toph!

17:40.110 --> 17:41.278
( SERPENT SCREECHES )

17:43.489 --> 17:45.574
-( PANTING )
- Help!

17:49.286 --> 17:50.704
( BUBBLING )

17:51.914 --> 17:53.207
( GASPS )

17:53.791 --> 17:56.835
Oh, Sokka, you saved me!

17:56.961 --> 17:58.796
Mwah!

17:58.879 --> 18:01.507
Actually, it's me.

18:01.590 --> 18:04.218
Oh, well. ( CHUCKLES )

18:04.301 --> 18:06.095
You can go ahead and
let me drown now.

18:07.596 --> 18:09.265
( ROARS )

18:17.231 --> 18:19.817
( SCREECHES )

18:22.736 --> 18:23.988
( SCREECHES )

18:30.786 --> 18:32.413
ALL: Yeah!

18:39.253 --> 18:40.254
There's the wall!

18:42.339 --> 18:45.467
Now it's nothing but smooth
sailing to Ba Sing Se.

18:45.551 --> 18:46.844
( GASPS ) Oh no!

18:46.927 --> 18:47.928
What's wrong?

18:48.637 --> 18:49.972
The baby's coming.

18:50.055 --> 18:51.598
What? Now?

18:51.682 --> 18:53.434
Can't you hold it in or something?

18:53.642 --> 18:54.810
Sokka, calm down.

18:54.893 --> 18:57.438
I helped Gran Gran deliver
lots of babies back home.

18:57.521 --> 19:00.441
This isn't the same as
delivering an arctic seal!

19:00.524 --> 19:03.861
This a real... Human... Thing!

19:04.320 --> 19:05.654
It's called a baby.

19:05.738 --> 19:07.990
And I've helped her deliver
plenty of those too.

19:08.073 --> 19:11.410
Aang, get some rags.
Sokka, water.

19:12.077 --> 19:15.497
Toph, I need you to make
an earth tent― A big one.

19:18.500 --> 19:19.752
Suki, come with me.

19:24.590 --> 19:26.967
You know, as soon
as I saw your scar,

19:27.051 --> 19:28.385
I knew exactly who you were.

19:29.970 --> 19:32.556
You're an outcast, like me.

19:32.639 --> 19:34.641
And us outcasts have
to stick together.

19:34.725 --> 19:39.188
We have to watch each other's
backs, because no one else will.

19:39.438 --> 19:43.400
I've realized lately that being on
your own isn't always the best path.

19:48.989 --> 19:51.700
( PANTING )

19:52.159 --> 19:55.079
You're doing great, Ying.
Sokka, where's that water?

19:55.329 --> 20:01.293
Now get ready to push.
One, two, three, push!

20:01.377 --> 20:03.379
( YING GROANS )

20:03.879 --> 20:05.839
( BABY CRYING )

20:05.923 --> 20:07.299
KATARA: It's a girl!

20:07.383 --> 20:09.385
So, you wanna go see the baby

20:09.468 --> 20:11.887
or are you going to faint
like an old lady again?

20:12.179 --> 20:13.847
No, no. I'm good this time.

20:20.437 --> 20:22.856
Aang, you have to come see this.

20:26.110 --> 20:27.319
( BABY CRYING )

20:27.486 --> 20:29.822
- She sounds healthy.
- She's beautiful.

20:30.781 --> 20:32.950
And so squishy-looking.

20:37.162 --> 20:38.580
What should we name her?

20:38.664 --> 20:41.583
I want our daughter's
name to be unique.

20:41.667 --> 20:43.585
I want it to mean something.

20:48.465 --> 20:51.260
I've been going through
a really hard time lately.

20:51.343 --> 20:53.679
But you've made
me hopeful again.

20:54.972 --> 20:57.057
I know what I want
to name our baby now.

20:57.766 --> 20:58.892
Hope.

20:59.393 --> 21:02.479
That's a perfect name. Hope.

21:06.233 --> 21:08.402
I thought I was
trying to be strong.

21:08.485 --> 21:11.363
But really I was just running
away from my feelings.

21:11.905 --> 21:15.993
Seeing this family together,
so full of happiness and love,

21:16.076 --> 21:18.454
it's reminding me
how I feel about Appa...

21:20.581 --> 21:22.416
...and how I feel about you.

21:30.299 --> 21:32.968
I promise, I'll find Appa
as fast as I can.

21:33.177 --> 21:34.803
I just really need to do this.

21:35.596 --> 21:37.055
See you in the big city.

21:37.139 --> 21:39.558
Say hi to that big fuzzball for me.

21:40.684 --> 21:43.061
- You'll find him, Aang.
- I know.

21:43.145 --> 21:44.354
Thank you, Katara.

21:46.356 --> 21:47.357
( CHATTERS )

21:47.441 --> 21:49.443
- You ready, Momo?
-( CHATTERS )

21:52.029 --> 21:53.989
( CHATTERS )

21:55.365 --> 21:57.576
Sokka, it's been really great
to see you again.

21:57.868 --> 21:59.328
Whoa, hold on.

21:59.411 --> 22:01.538
Why does it sound like
you're saying goodbye?

22:01.622 --> 22:03.665
I came along because
I wanted to make sure

22:03.749 --> 22:05.876
you got through
the Serpent's Pass safely.

22:05.959 --> 22:08.670
But now I need to get back
to the other Kyoshi Warriors.

22:08.921 --> 22:11.715
So you came along to protect me?

22:11.840 --> 22:15.886
Listen, I'm really sorry about last night.

22:16.303 --> 22:19.473
We were talking and saying things...

22:19.556 --> 22:21.850
I just got carried away
and before I knew it, I―

22:24.353 --> 22:25.729
You talk too much.

22:33.612 --> 22:35.239
( MOMO CHATTERS )

22:39.535 --> 22:40.536
( CHATTERS )

22:46.583 --> 22:47.834
( CHATTERS )

22:52.047 --> 22:53.298
( GASPS )

23:05.310 --> 23:08.021
Sorry, Momo. Appa's gonna have to wait.

23:08.355 --> 23:09.856
( DRILL WHIRRING )
